    "sourcePrompt": "Three-column time-echo split effect using Canvas rendering to avoid black frames. One main video element + two seek-only auxiliary videos + one full-frame canvas overlay. THREE split events in this 30s clip\nHTML STRUCTURE\n#mainVideo: the backgroundVideo, plays normally, controls the master clock. position:absolute, width:100%, height:100%, object-fit:cover, z-index:0\n#auxVideo1: same src as backgroundVideo, muted, preload:auto, NOT playing (no .play() call), used only for canvas seek. position:absolute, left:-9999px, width:1px, height:1px, visibility:hidden\n#auxVideo2: same as auxVideo1. Hidden off-screen\n#splitCanvas: position:absolute, top:0, left:0, width:100%, height:100%, z-index:1, pointer-events:none. Visible only during split events, otherwise display:none\n#barLeft, #barRight: two black divider bars, position:absolute, z-index:2, width:10px, height:100%, background:#000, box-shadow:0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.45). barLeft at left:calc(33.33% - 5px), barRight at left:calc(66.67% - 5px). Hidden between events\n#splitWrapper: wraps #splitCanvas + #barLeft + #barRight. opacity controlled for enter/exit\nCANVAS RENDERING LOOP (runs every requestAnimationFrame while split is active)\nconst ctx = splitCanvas.getContext('2d')\nconst W = splitCanvas.width; // match container pixel width\nconst H = splitCanvas.height; // match container pixel height\n// Seek aux videos to offset times (do NOT call .play())\nauxVideo1.currentTime = mainVideo.currentTime + 0.3\nauxVideo2.currentTime = mainVideo.currentTime + 0.6\n// Draw three columns\nctx.drawImage(mainVideo,  0,       0, W/3, H,   0,       0, W/3, H); // left: current frame\nctx.drawImage(auxVideo1,  W/3,     0, W/3, H,   W/3,     0, W/3, H); // center: +0.3s\nctx.drawImage(auxVideo2,  W*2/3,   0, W/3, H,   W*2/3,   0, W/3, H); // right: +0.6s\nNote: drawImage source rect mirrors the destination rect so each column shows only its own third of the frame — creating a true three-column split of the full-width video\nSPLIT ENTER — 3 trigger times: t=3.0s, t=12.0s, t=22.0s\nShow #splitWrapper (display:block), animate opacity 0→1 over 0.15s easeOut\nShow #barLeft and #barRight, animate translateX: barLeft from -100% to 0, barRight from +100% to 0, 0.15s easeOut\nStart canvas rAF loop\nHide #mainVideo (opacity 0) so canvas fully replaces it visually\nSCENE-CUT DETECTION for EXIT (runs during hold)\nUse a separate tiny 64×36 canvas (#detectCanvas, hidden)\nEach rAF: draw mainVideo onto detectCanvas, read getImageData, compute avg luminance\nIf |luminance - prevLuminance| > 18 → scene cut detected → trigger EXIT\nFallback: EXIT after 4.0s hold if no cut detected\nSPLIT EXIT — on scene cut or 4s fallback\nAnimate #splitWrapper opacity 1→0 over 0.15s easeIn (single parent transition, NO per-element stagger)\nSimultaneously animate barLeft translateX(0→-100%) and barRight translateX(0→+100%), 0.15s easeIn\nAfter 0.15s: stop rAF loop, hide #splitWrapper (display:none), show #mainVideo (opacity 1)\nBETWEEN EVENTS\n#splitWrapper: display:none. #mainVideo: visible, opacity:1, playing normally\nNo text, no captions, no labels, no UI chrome of any kind",
